Botium Toys: Scope, Goals, and Risk Assessment Report
Scope
The audit covers the entire security program, including all assets, internal processes, and compliance practices.

Goals
Assess existing assets and complete the controls/compliance checklist to determine which improvements are needed.

Current Assets
On‑premises equipment

Employee devices

Storefront products and warehouse inventory

Systems/software: accounting, telecom, database, security, ecommerce, inventory

Internet access

Internal network

Data retention/storage

Legacy systems requiring manual monitoring

Risk Assessment
Risk Description
Botium Toys lacks proper controls and may not be fully compliant with U.S. and international standards.

Control Best Practices
Following the NIST CSF Identify function, Botium Toys must classify and manage assets and determine business continuity impact.

Risk Score
8/10 (High) — due to missing controls and compliance gaps.

Additional Comments
Key issues include:

All employees can access sensitive data (cardholder, PII/SPII).

No encryption for credit card data.

No least privilege or separation of duties.

Firewall and antivirus exist.

No IDS.

No disaster recovery plan or backups.

EU breach notification plan exists.

Weak password policy.

No centralized password management.

Legacy systems lack scheduled maintenance.

Physical security is sufficient (locks, CCTV, fire systems).
